  "statement": "Use the Newton-Raphson method with $x_{0}=1$ to find $x_{1}$ and $x_{2}$ for the equation $x^{3}-x-1=0$, and state the root correct to four decimal places.",
  "solution": "$f(x)=x^{3}-x-1$, $f'(x)=3x^{2}-1$. $x_{0}=1$: $f(1)=-1$, $f'(1)=2$, so $x_{1}=1-\\\\tfrac{-1}{2}=1.5$. $x_{1}=1.5$: $f=3.375-1.5-1=0.875$, $f'=6.75-1=5.75$, so $x_{2}=1.5-\\\\tfrac{0.875}{5.75}\\\\approx1.34783$. The root is $x\\\\approx1.3247$.",
